From cc03378a71901a89841a8e38f99de6e2530ae480 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:35:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(auth): add public homepage and self-serve signup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WelliPay previously had no public-facing entry point — any visit
immediately rendered a bare login form with no way to create an account.
This adds the pieces to run WelliPay as its own product:

- src/pages/Homepage.tsx: public marketing landing page (hero, feature
  grid, how-it-works, CTA) shown at "/" for signed-out visitors.
- src/components/Signup.tsx: self-serve provider signup — collects
  hospital/clinic name, work email, and password, creates a Firebase
  Auth account, and signs the user straight in.
- AuthContext: added a `signup` method (createUserWithEmailAndPassword +
  displayName) alongside the existing `login`.
- App.tsx: real routes for "/", "/login", "/signup" that redirect a
  signed-in visitor straight to the dashboard instead of showing the
  marketing/auth pages again; unauthenticated visitors hitting an app
  route are redirected to /login instead of getting Login rendered
  inline, so the URL always matches what's on screen.
- Login.tsx: added a link to the new signup page.

Also fixes a real, pre-existing CSS bug this surfaced: index.css set
h1-h4 heading color in a bare, unlayered rule, which — under Tailwind's
cascade-layer rules — always wins over any `text-*` color utility
applied directly to a heading tag, regardless of specificity. That
silently broke the new homepage's white-on-navy CTA heading, and would
break any future heading that isn't the default navy. Fixed by moving
the rule into `@layer base` so utility overrides work as expected.

Verified: tsc --noEmit clean, production build succeeds, and all three
pages (homepage, login, signup) render correctly at desktop and mobile
viewports (screenshotted via Playwright against the built app).

